<div class="d-flex justify-content-center">

  <div class="card" style="width: 60rem; background: #f2f4f6">
    <div class="card-body">
      <div class="d-flex justify-content-center mb-3">
        <%= image_tag("aji.jpg", width:"750px", class:"figure-img img-fluid rounded")%>
      </div>
      <h3 class="card-title mb-5 text-center">About</h3>
      <h4 class="card-text mb-3">
        This app was inspired by my mischievous cat, Aji — a ginger-and-white furball with a surprisingly picky palate. 
        Unlike most ginger cats, Aji has his own unique favorites. For example, he loves chicken more than tuna or salmon.
      </h4>
      <h4 class="card-text mb-3">
        How do I know? I used to track his meals in an Excel sheet, and over time, I started noticing patterns. 
        If I served him something he didn’t like… he’d skip the meal entirely (me: 😅).
      </h4>
      <h4 class="card-text mb-3">
        You might say I spoil him — and you'd be absolutely right. I love Aji, and I want him to enjoy every single meal.
        But using Excel was tedious — every input was manual, and there was no easy way to visualize trends over time. 
        So, I built this app: a smarter way to track meals, spot preferences, and keep Aji well-fed and happy.
      </h4>
      <h4 class="card-text mb-3">
        ✨ Want to join me? Sign up and try it yourself:  
      </h4>
      <h5 class="card-text mb-3">👉 <a href="https://feeding-tracker-v2-3e86df55d613.herokuapp.com/signup" class="btn btn-secondary">Sign Up</a></h5>
      <h5>If you're interested in learning more about cat eating behavior, 
      I highly recommend consulting a professional. I personally found great insights from <a href="https://www.petbuddytraining.com/">Pet Buddy Training</a>.
      </h5>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>